    "tests/fidelity/attrs.mjs": "import {chromium} from '@playwright/test';\nconst [,, url, sel] = process.argv;\nconst b=await chromium.launch();const p=await b.newPage({viewport:{width:1440,height:900}});\nawait p.goto(url);await p.evaluate(()=>{localStorage.setItem('km-meet-theme','dark');localStorage.setItem('km-auth',JSON.stringify({name:'Avery Chen',email:'avery@example.com'}))});\nawait p.goto(url);await p.reload();await p.waitForTimeout(1200);\nconsole.log(await p.evaluate((sel)=>[...document.querySelectorAll(sel)].map(e=>e.tagName+' '+[...e.attributes].map(a=>a.name+'='+a.value.slice(0,40)).join(' ')).join('\\n'),sel));await b.close();\n",
    "tests/fidelity/baseline-defects.md": "# c13 Stage B reference defects \u2014 2026-11-13\n\nThis is an evidence report and proposed correction, not a baseline amendment.\nNo baseline, frozen threshold or acceptance rule was changed for this report.\n\n## Authority and uncomfortable finding\n\nThe adopted contract digest is\n`261ec2fd7ff96c0deaa35a4d59f8723858ecdcdeec2e417e0e090c27d7bec7b6`.\nIts VS-1 baseline-set digest is\n`00d11d22e84a6f8910c8d5fb016097b26c68e1187a41e2c59c11e6960e166e5d`.\nThe last complete saved run failed 54 scenarios and 324 screenshot cells.\nMost failures remain implementation work. At least two reference problems mean\nfaithful product behavior alone cannot reproduce every frozen image reliably.\n\n## 1. Schedule preview contains an unseeded code and temporary server address\n\nAffected state: `dashboard.schedule`, both themes, all four widths. All eight\ncells failed in the last saved run; this does not attribute every pixel failure\nin those cells to this defect.\n\nRepresentative frozen image:\n`tests/fidelity/baselines/dark/1024/dashboard-schedule.png`.\nSaved comparison directory:\n`/private/tmp/km-vs1c/test-results/vs-1-web-fidelity.feature--876a4-hemes-at-all-four-viewports-web/dark/1024/`.\nFiles there are `dashboard-schedule-expected.png`,\n`dashboard-schedule-actual.png`, and `dashboard-schedule-diff.png`.\n\nThe expected preview displays\n`http://127.0.0.1:65160/prototype/join.html#invite?code=km-vrm-euq`;\nthe saved app preview displays\n`http://127.0.0.1:4180/join#invite?code=km-gyf-ect`.\nThese differences change wrapping, card height and SMS character count.\n\nSource evidence:\n\n- `docs/design/prototype/dashboard.html` generates codes with `Math.random()`\n  and resolves `join.html` relative to `location.href`.\n- `apps/web/src/presentation/dashboard/application/dashboard-fixtures.ts`\n  generates codes with `Math.random()` and uses the real app's `/join` route.\n- `tests/fidelity/src/support/capture-environment.ts` freezes the clock but\n  does not seed randomness or normalize the display origin.\n- `tests/fidelity/src/capture/static-server.ts` chooses the serving origin at\n  runtime. The frozen image therefore contains an ephemeral environment value.\n\nProposed correction, requiring design-lead adjudication and operator adoption:\ndefine one deterministic schedule fixture for both prototype and app capture,\nwith a fixed join code and a stable display origin/route. Supply it at the\ncapture boundary before preview text, wrapping and SMS count are calculated.\nKeep ordinary product link generation unchanged. Recapture only the eight\nschedule cells, review the pairs, update their image hashes and the baseline-set\ndigest, then bind a signed VS-1 reference amendment. Retain original images and\nreceipts. Do not raise thresholds or mask layout differences.\n\nAn R3 mask of only dynamic text is an alternative under the frozen rubric, but\ndoes not solve wrapping and count changes by itself. It is not recommended here.\n\n## 2. Processing reference at 768 shows the phone navigation\n\nFrozen image:\n`tests/fidelity/baselines/light/768/recordings-processing-partner-onboarding-1014.png`.\nSaved comparison directory:\n`/private/tmp/km-vs1c/test-results/vs-1-web-fidelity.feature--82cfa-hemes-at-all-four-viewports-web/light/768/`.\nIts expected/actual/diff filenames begin\n`recordings-processing-partner-onboarding-1014-`.\n\nThe expected image shows the five-item bottom bar and content starting at x=24.\nThe app image shows the rail and content starting at x=104. At width 768 the\nrail is correct under DESIGN.md's 600\u20131023 medium range. The baseline's\nnotification switch is checked; its fill at (680, 375) is RGB (193, 62, 30).\nAn earlier visual reading of a grey track was incorrect and is superseded by\nthe image bytes. Switch rendering is not a reference-defect claim here.\n\nThe manifest identifies this cell as viewport 768, full-page capture, using\n`/prototype/recordings.html?km-processing-pin=2#processing:partner-onboarding-1014`.\nThe shared capture environment sets its viewport to 768\u00d71024.\nThe prototype's `km.js` uses `navClassFor(window.innerWidth)` with medium=600\nand expanded=1024, so its source requires a rail at 768. The processing source\nsets the notification checkbox to `checked: true`.\n\nThe current baseline and the run3 `-expected.png` both hash to\n`82594af1edb25dbd3bc5e26c8f7e79dfa231b98c89d6b8b1a2881dbb6048bbc3`,\nmatching the manifest; both are 768\u00d71031. The saved `-actual.png` hashes to\n`ce27f0f8f1001060572af3d5f4ff6b12f976e7eeb126f6fed4d3885dad57bbd0`.\n\nThe underlying cause has not been reproduced. Possible transient rendering is\nan investigation hypothesis, not a finding. A baseline screenshot cannot prove\nits DOM state or timing. This is an inconsistent reference image, not grounds\nto change the product to a bottom bar at 768.\n\nProposed correction: capture this one prototype cell into a scratch evidence\ndirectory using the existing clock, fonts and processing pin. Before capture,\nrecord viewport dimensions, `data-nav-class=rail`, the checked input and its\ncomputed track fill. Compare the scratch image with the frozen image and obtain\ndesign-lead approval before replacing this one baseline and amending its digest.\nDo not recapture unrelated cells or change navigation breakpoints.\n\n## 3. Fixed-navigation full-page difference needs diagnosis\n\n`frame.nav-rail` at 768, both themes: the saved expected image's rail background\ncontinues through the full long page; the app image's rail background stops at\nthe initial viewport. The first content page-height differences are separately\nimplementation defects; a full-page background mismatch alone does not establish\nwhich image is wrong.\n\nStatic parity evidence: baseline `captureJob()` and app `renderAndCompare()` both\nuse shared `driveState()` and `captureSubject()` with `fullPage: true`, animations\ndisabled and CSS-pixel scale. Both call the Playwright screenshot implementation.\nThe installed Playwright 1.65 Chromium implementation uses CDP\n`Page.captureScreenshot` with `captureBeyondViewport`; it does not explicitly\nresize the page viewport in that path. The baseline manifest records the same\nPlaywright version. Both prototype and app nav rules are fixed with top/bottom.\n\nNo harness workaround is justified by this static evidence. Compare computed\ncontaining blocks and capture state at the authorized boundary before changing\ncode or proposing a reference correction.\n\n## 4. Home footer includes a prototype-only catalog link\n\nThe prototype footer includes `All screens` linking to its screen catalog, plus\nseparator dots. The application has no corresponding user-facing route. The\ndelivery lead explicitly preserves that omission rather than inventing a debug\nscreen in the product. Its home-page footer layout can be corrected separately,\nbut this content difference needs a narrow reference adjudication if it remains\noutside the frozen threshold. Do not add a broken or fabricated product link.\n\n## Evidence and budget preservation\n\n- Initial complete VS-1 run: `/private/tmp/km-vs1/playwright.json`, started\n  2026-11-12T21:52:42.649Z, 61 failed and 13 passed.\n- First retry: `stageb-vs1-fidelity-run2.log`, stopped by SIGTERM after 16 tests;\n  `/private/tmp/km-vs1b` has no complete Playwright JSON receipt.\n- Second retry: `/private/tmp/km-vs1c/playwright.json`, started\n  2026-11-13T01:13:51.484Z, 54 failed and 20 passed, duration 823013.37 ms.\n- VS-4: `/private/tmp/km-vs4/playwright.json`, started\n  2026-11-12T21:58:21.290Z, 3 passed, duration 7844.904 ms.\n\nThe two retry invocations consume at least two of the contract's three repair\nattempts; interruption does not reset consumption. No complete phase-wide\ntime/tool-call/repair ledger was found. These are historical observations, not\nfresh certification of the dirty current working tree. The Playwright reports\nlack a complete source/build fingerprint. Their stored timestamps and files\nmust be retained; they cannot be relabelled as a new candidate's results.\n",
    "tests/fidelity/cs.mjs": "import {chromium} from '@playwright/test';\nconst [,, url, sel, props] = process.argv;\nconst b=await chromium.launch();const p=await b.newPage({viewport:{width:1440,height:900}});\nawait p.goto(url);await p.evaluate(()=>{localStorage.setItem('km-meet-theme','dark')});await p.reload();await p.waitForTimeout(600);\nconsole.log(await p.evaluate(([sel,props])=>{const e=document.querySelector(sel);if(!e)return 'none';const cs=getComputedStyle(e);return props.split(',').map(k=>k+': '+cs.getPropertyValue(k)).join(' | ')},[sel,props]));await b.close();\n",
    "tests/fidelity/cs3.mjs": "import {chromium} from '@playwright/test';\nconst [,, url, sel, props] = process.argv;\nconst b=await chromium.launch();const p=await b.newPage({viewport:{width:1440,height:900}});\nawait p.goto(url);await p.evaluate(()=>{localStorage.setItem('km-meet-theme','dark');localStorage.setItem('km-auth',JSON.stringify({name:'Avery Chen',email:'avery@example.com'}))});await p.goto(url);await p.reload();await p.waitForTimeout(1500);\nconsole.log(await p.evaluate(([sel,props])=>{const e=document.querySelector(sel);if(!e)return 'none';const cs=getComputedStyle(e);return props.split(',').map(k=>k+': '+cs.getPropertyValue(k)).join(' | ')},[sel,props]));await b.close();\n",
    "tests/fidelity/geo.mjs": "import {chromium} from '@playwright/test';\nconst [,, url, sel, w] = process.argv;\nconst b=await chromium.launch();const p=await b.newPage({viewport:{width:+w||1440,height:900}});\nawait p.goto(url);await p.waitForTimeout(800);\nconst r=await p.evaluate((sel)=>[...document.querySelectorAll(sel)].map(e=>{const r=e.getBoundingClientRect();const cs=getComputedStyle(e);return `${e.tagName}.${e.className.toString().slice(0,40)} x=${r.x.toFixed(1)} y=${r.y.toFixed(1)} w=${r.width.toFixed(1)} h=${r.height.toFixed(1)} pad=${cs.padding} mar=${cs.margin} gap=${cs.gap}`}),sel);\nconsole.log(r.join('\\n'));await b.close();\n",
    "tests/fidelity/geo2.mjs": "import {chromium} from '@playwright/test';\nconst [,, url, sel, w] = process.argv;\nconst b=await chromium.launch();const p=await b.newPage({viewport:{width:+w||1440,height:900}});\nawait p.goto(url);await p.evaluate(()=>{localStorage.setItem('km-meet-theme','dark')});await p.reload();await p.waitForTimeout(800);\nconst r=await p.evaluate((sel)=>[...document.querySelectorAll(sel)].map(e=>{const r=e.getBoundingClientRect();return `${e.tagName}${e.id?'#'+e.id:''}.${(e.className.toString()||'').slice(0,30)} y=${(r.y+scrollY).toFixed(0)} h=${r.height.toFixed(0)} x=${r.x.toFixed(0)} w=${r.width.toFixed(0)} :: ${(e.textContent||'').trim().slice(0,28).replace(/\\s+/g,' ')}`}),sel);\nconsole.log(r.join('\\n'));console.log('docH',await p.evaluate(()=>document.documentElement.scrollHeight));await b.close();\n",
    "tests/fidelity/geo3.mjs": "import {chromium} from '@playwright/test';\nconst [,, url, sel, w] = process.argv;\nconst b=await chromium.launch();const p=await b.newPage({viewport:{width:+w||1440,height:900}});\nawait p.goto(url);await p.evaluate(()=>{localStorage.setItem('km-meet-theme','dark');localStorage.setItem('km-auth',JSON.stringify({name:'Avery Chen',email:'avery@example.com'}))});await p.goto(url);await p.reload();await p.waitForTimeout(1500);\nconst r=await p.evaluate((sel)=>[...document.querySelectorAll(sel)].map(e=>{const r=e.getBoundingClientRect();return `${e.tagName}${e.id?'#'+e.id:''}.${(e.className.toString()||'').slice(0,30)} y=${(r.y+scrollY).toFixed(0)} h=${r.height.toFixed(0)} x=${r.x.toFixed(0)} w=${r.width.toFixed(0)} :: ${(e.textContent||'').trim().slice(0,28).replace(/\\s+/g,' ')}`}),sel);\nconsole.log(r.join('\\n'));console.log('docH',await p.evaluate(()=>document.documentElement.scrollHeight));await b.close();\n",
    "tests/fidelity/src/bundle-identity/embedded-assets.ts": "/**\n * Reads the web assets a built Tauri 2 app actually serves, straight from its\n * executable (VS-2 strengthening, c13 Stage B).\n *\n * Tauri embeds every `frontendDist` file in the binary as a standalone brotli\n * stream (tauri-codegen, `compression` feature, WBITS 22 in every stream's\n * first byte: low nibble 0xB). Streams carry no length or magic number, but\n * each one is self-terminating, so a scan that tries the decoder at every\n * candidate offset recovers the original bytes of every embedded file. The\n * result is keyed by sha256 so it does not depend on Tauri's private layout,\n * the compression quality (debug 2, release 9) or the asset table order.\n *\n * HTML is the one asset Tauri rewrites before embedding (parse and\n * re-serialise: doctype case, attribute quoting, entity decoding), so HTML is\n * compared by its token structure instead of by bytes (`normalizeHtml`).\n */\nimport { readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { brotliDecompressSync } from \"node:zlib\";\nimport { sha256 } from \"../support/digests.ts\";\n\nconst WBITS_22_LOW_NIBBLE = 0x0b;\nconst MAX_ASSET_BYTES = 64 * 1024 * 1024;\n\nexport interface EmbeddedBlob {\n  readonly offset: number;\n  readonly sha256: string;\n  readonly bytes: Buffer;\n}\n\n/** Every brotli stream in `binary` that decodes to a non-empty payload. */\nexport function scanEmbeddedBlobs(binary: Buffer): EmbeddedBlob[] {\n  const blobs: EmbeddedBlob[] = [];\n  const skipUntil = 0;\n  for (let offset = 0; offset < binary.length - 1; offset += 1) {\n    if (offset < skipUntil || ((binary[offset] ?? 0) & 0x0f) !== WBITS_22_LOW_NIBBLE) continue;\n    let bytes: Buffer;\n    try {\n      bytes = brotliDecompressSync(binary.subarray(offset), { maxOutputLength: MAX_ASSET_BYTES });\n    } catch {\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (bytes.length === 0) continue;\n    blobs.push({ offset, sha256: sha256(bytes), bytes });\n  }\n  return blobs;\n}\n\n/** Locates the executable inside a macOS `.app` (Contents/MacOS has one file). */\nexport function appExecutable(app: string): string {\n  const dir = join(app, \"Contents\", \"MacOS\");\n  const names = readdirSync(dir).filter((n) => statSync(join(dir, n)).isFile());\n  const [first] = names;\n  if (names.length !== 1 || first === undefined)\n    throw new Error(`${dir} must hold exactly one executable (found ${names.length})`);\n  return join(dir, first);\n}\n\ninterface HtmlToken {\n  readonly kind: \"tag\" | \"text\" | \"comment\";\n  readonly value: string;\n}\n\nconst entities: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = {\n  \"&#39;\": \"'\",\n  \"&apos;\": \"'\",\n  \"&quot;\": '\"',\n  \"&lt;\": \"<\",\n  \"&gt;\": \">\",\n  \"&amp;\": \"&\",\n};\n\nconst decodeEntities = (s: string): string =>\n  s.replace(/&(#39|apos|quot|lt|gt|amp);/g, (m) => entities[m] ?? m);\n\nfunction normalizeAttributes(source: string): string {\n  const attrs: string[] = [];\n  const pattern = /([^\\s=/>]+)(?:\\s*=\\s*(?:\"([^\"]*)\"|'([^']*)'|([^\\s>]+)))?/g;\n  for (const match of source.matchAll(pattern)) {\n    const value = match[2] ?? match[3] ?? match[4] ?? \"\";\n    attrs.push(`${(match[1] ?? \"\").toLowerCase()}=${JSON.stringify(decodeEntities(value))}`);\n  }\n  return attrs.sort().join(\" \");\n}\n\n/**\n * Structure of an HTML document as comparable tokens: lower-cased tag names\n * with sorted, entity-decoded attributes; non-blank text and comments with\n * runs of whitespace collapsed. Insensitive to the serialisation changes\n * Tauri applies, sensitive to any change of element, attribute or text.\n */\nexport function normalizeHtml(html: string): string[] {\n  const tokens: HtmlToken[] = [];\n  const pattern =\n    /<!--([\\s\\S]*?)-->|<!doctype\\s+([^>]*)>|<(\\/?)([a-zA-Z][^\\s/>]*)([^>]*?)\\/?>|([^<]+)/gi;\n  for (const m of html.matchAll(pattern)) {\n    if (m[1] !== undefined)\n      tokens.push({ kind: \"comment\", value: m[1].replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim() });\n    else if (m[2] !== undefined)\n      tokens.push({ kind: \"tag\", value: `!doctype ${m[2].trim().toLowerCase()}` });\n    else if (m[4] !== undefined)\n      tokens.push({\n        kind: \"tag\",\n        value: `${m[3] ?? \"\"}${m[4].toLowerCase()} ${normalizeAttributes(m[5] ?? \"\")}`.trim(),\n      });\n    else if (m[6] !== undefined && m[6].trim() !== \"\")\n      tokens.push({ kind: \"text\", value: decodeEntities(m[6]).replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim() });\n  }\n  return tokens.map((t) => `${t.kind}:${t.value}`);\n}\n\nexport const sameHtml = (a: string, b: string): boolean =>\n  JSON.stringify(normalizeHtml(a)) === JSON.stringify(normalizeHtml(b));\n\nexport function readEmbedded(app: string): EmbeddedBlob[] {\n  return scanEmbeddedBlobs(readFileSync(appExecutable(app)));\n}\n",
    "tests/fidelity/src/support/candidate-snapshot.ts": "import { execFileSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport {\n  chmodSync,\n  lstatSync,\n  mkdirSync,\n  readFileSync,\n  readlinkSync,\n  rmSync,\n  symlinkSync,\n  writeFileSync,\n} from \"node:fs\";\nimport { dirname, join } from \"node:path\";\n\n// These are workflow records and runner outputs, never production build inputs.\nconst EXCLUDED_ROOTS = [\n  \".agent-team/\",\n  \".agents/\",\n  \".claude/\",\n  \".codex/\",\n  \".dsh/\",\n  \".kbd-orchestrator/\",\n  \".kimi-code/\",\n  \".opencode/\",\n  \".prometheus/\",\n  \".qwen/\",\n  \".zed/\",\n  \"reports/\",\n  \"test-results/\",\n  \"playwright-report/\",\n  \"tests/fidelity/.features-gen/\",\n  \"tests/fidelity/reports/\",\n] as const;\n\ninterface CandidateFile {\n  readonly path: string;\n  readonly kind: \"file\" | \"symlink\" | \"deleted\";\n  readonly mode: number;\n  readonly content: Buffer;\n}\n\nexport interface CandidateSnapshot {\n  readonly head: string;\n  readonly files: readonly CandidateFile[];\n  readonly digest: string;\n  readonly receipt: string;\n}\n\nfunction git(root: string, args: readonly string[]): string {\n  return execFileSync(\"git\", [...args], { cwd: root, encoding: \"utf8\" });\n}\n\n/** Captures dirty tracked inputs and nonignored new inputs, including deletions. */\nexport function captureCandidate(root: string): CandidateSnapshot {\n  const head = git(root, [\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"]).trim();\n  const paths = new Set(\n    [\n      git(root, [\"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"-z\", \"HEAD\", \"--\"]),\n      git(root, [\"ls-files\", \"--others\", \"--exclude-standard\", \"-z\"]),\n    ]\n      .join(\"\\0\")\n      .split(\"\\0\")\n      .filter((path) => path !== \"\" && !EXCLUDED_ROOTS.some((prefix) => path.startsWith(prefix))),\n  );\n  const files: CandidateFile[] = [...paths].sort().map((path) => {\n    const source = join(root, path);\n    const stat = lstatSync(source, { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n    if (stat === undefined)\n      return { path, kind: \"deleted\", mode: 0, content: Buffer.alloc(0) };\n    if (stat.isSymbolicLink())\n      return { path, kind: \"symlink\", mode: 0, content: Buffer.from(readlinkSync(source)) };\n    if (!stat.isFile()) throw new Error(`Candidate input is not a file: ${path}`);\n    return { path, kind: \"file\", mode: stat.mode & 0o777, content: readFileSync(source) };\n  });\n  const inputs = files.map(({ path, kind, mode, content }) => ({\n    path,\n    kind,\n    mode,\n    sha256: createHash(\"sha256\").update(content).digest(\"hex\"),\n  }));\n  const identity = { head, inputs, excludedRoots: EXCLUDED_ROOTS };\n  const digest = createHash(\"sha256\").update(JSON.stringify(identity)).digest(\"hex\");\n  return { head, files, digest, receipt: JSON.stringify({ ...identity, digest }, null, 2) };\n}\n\n/** Applies the captured overlay only inside the isolated scratch checkout. */\nexport function applyCandidate(snapshot: CandidateSnapshot, destination: string): void {\n  for (const file of snapshot.files) {\n    const path = join(destination, file.path);\n    rmSync(path, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    if (file.kind === \"deleted\") continue;\n    mkdirSync(dirname(path), { recursive: true });\n    if (file.kind === \"symlink\") symlinkSync(file.content.toString(), path);\n    else {\n      writeFileSync(path, file.content);\n      chmodSync(path, file.mode);\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
  },
  "source_context": {
    "tests/fidelity/src/support/scratch-worktree.ts": "import { mkdtempSync, rmSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { tmpdir } from \"node:os\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { applyCandidate, captureCandidate } from \"./candidate-snapshot.ts\";\nimport { REPO_ROOT } from \"./repo-paths.ts\";\nimport { runCommand } from \"./run-command.ts\";\n\n/**\n * A detached worktree overlaid with the current candidate's uncommitted inputs,\n * used by negative controls (\"scratch branch\" in the contract). The committed\n * tree and working copy are never modified. Always call `remove()`.\n */\nexport interface ScratchWorktree {\n  readonly dir: string;\n  readonly candidateReceipt: string;\n  remove(): void;\n}\n\nexport function createScratchWorktree(label: string): ScratchWorktree {\n  const candidate = captureCandidate(REPO_ROOT);\n  const parent = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), `km-${label}-`));\n  const dir = join(parent, \"tree\");\n  const added = runCommand(`git worktree add --detach \"${dir}\" ${candidate.head}`, REPO_ROOT);\n  if (added.exitCode !== 0) throw new Error(`git worktree add failed: ${added.stderr}`);\n  const remove = (): void => {\n    runCommand(`git worktree remove --force \"${dir}\"`, REPO_ROOT);\n    rmSync(parent, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  };\n  try {\n    applyCandidate(candidate, dir);\n    // A concurrent edit would otherwise give the control a different candidate.\n    if (captureCandidate(REPO_ROOT).digest !== candidate.digest)\n      throw new Error(\"Candidate changed while preparing the negative-control checkout\");\n    return { dir, candidateReceipt: candidate.receipt, remove };\n  } catch (error) {\n    remove();\n    throw error;\n  }\n}\n\n/** Installs dependencies from the candidate lockfile overlaid into the scratch worktree. */\nexport function installScratch(dir: string): void {\n  const install = runCommand(\"pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --prefer-offline\", dir);\n  if (install.exitCode !== 0)\n    throw new Error(`scratch install failed: ${install.stderr.slice(-2000)}`);\n}\n\nexport function scratchTempDir(label: string): { dir: string; remove(): void } {\n  const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), `km-${label}-`));\n  return { dir, remove: () => rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true }) };\n}\n",
    "tests/fidelity/steps/token-propagation.steps.ts": "import { cpSync, existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { expect } from \"@playwright/test\";\nimport { listFiles } from \"../src/support/digests.ts\";\nimport { repoPath } from \"../src/support/repo-paths.ts\";\nimport { combinedOutput } from \"../src/support/run-command.ts\";\nimport { scratchTempDir } from \"../src/support/scratch-worktree.ts\";\nimport { lastRun, runAndRecord } from \"./common.steps.ts\";\nimport { Given, type ScenarioState, Then, When } from \"./fixtures.ts\";\n\n/**\n * Generator interface (packages/design-tokens/generator/src/cli.ts): the only\n * inputs are `--config <path>` and `--check`. Paths in the config resolve\n * relative to the config file and output directories must already exist. Each\n * run here writes a scratch config that points `source` at the scratch\n * tokens.json and every output (web CSS, shadcn variables, Tailwind @theme,\n * Dart tokens/ThemeData, brand CSS, manifest) into a scratch directory; fonts\n * are read from the real package (read-only). The generator exits non-zero on\n * an invalid value or a missing output directory.\n */\nconst GENERATE = \"pnpm --filter @know-meet/design-tokens generate\";\nconst REAL_CONFIG = repoPath(\"packages/design-tokens/token-generator.config.json\");\n\ninterface GeneratorConfigFile {\n  readonly fonts: { readonly dir: string };\n  readonly outputs: {\n    readonly flutter: Record<string, unknown>;\n    readonly brandDocs: Record<string, unknown>;\n  };\n}\n\n/** Writes a scratch config whose outputs live under `outDir` (created unless `create` is false). */\nfunction scratchConfig(s: TokenScratch, outDir: string, create: boolean): string {\n  const real = JSON.parse(readFileSync(REAL_CONFIG, \"utf8\")) as GeneratorConfigFile;\n  const realDir = join(REAL_CONFIG, \"..\");\n  for (const sub of [\"web\", \"flutter\"])\n    if (create) mkdirSync(join(outDir, sub), { recursive: true });\n  const config = {\n    ...real,\n    source: s.tokens,\n    fonts: { ...real.fonts, dir: join(realDir, real.fonts.dir) },\n    outputs: {\n      ...real.outputs,\n      web: { dir: join(outDir, \"web\") },\n      flutter: { ...real.outputs.flutter, dir: join(outDir, \"flutter\") },\n      brandDocs: { ...real.outputs.brandDocs, file: join(outDir, \"brand-tokens.css\") },\n      manifest: join(outDir, \"manifest.json\"),\n    },\n  };\n  const path = join(s.root, `${outDir.split(\"/\").pop()}.config.json`);\n  writeFileSync(path, `${JSON.stringify(config, null, 2)}\\n`);\n  return path;\n}\n\nconst generateInto = (s: TokenScratch, outDir: string, create = true): string =>\n  `${GENERATE} --config \"${scratchConfig(s, outDir, create)}\"`;\n\ninterface TokenScratch {\n  readonly tokens: string;\n  readonly baselineOut: string;\n  readonly out: string;\n  readonly root: string;\n}\n\nconst scratches = new WeakMap<ScenarioState, TokenScratch>();\n\nfunction scratchOf(scenario: ScenarioState): TokenScratch {\n  const value = scratches.get(scenario);\n  if (value === undefined) throw new Error(\"No scratch tokens.json in this scenario\");\n  return value;\n}\n\nfunction changedLines(before: string, after: string): Array<{ file: string; line: string }> {\n  const out: Array<{ file: string; line: string }> = [];\n  const files = new Set([...listFiles(before), ...listFiles(after)]);\n  for (const file of files) {\n    const a = existsSync(join(before, file))\n      ? readFileSync(join(before, file), \"utf8\").split(\"\\n\")\n      : [];\n    const b = existsSync(join(after, file))\n      ? readFileSync(join(after, file), \"utf8\").split(\"\\n\")\n      : [];\n    const length = Math.max(a.length, b.length);\n    for (let index = 0; index < length; index += 1)\n      if (a[index] !== b[index])\n        out.push({ file, line: b[index] ?? `<removed> ${a[index] ?? \"\"}` });\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\n/**\n * Output lines that differ, excluding manifest.json: it records each scratch\n * output's absolute-ish path and digest, so it differs by construction. Its\n * file list (names, not directories) must still be identical.\n */\nfunction tokenOutputChanges(before: string, after: string): Array<{ file: string; line: string }> {\n  const names = (dir: string): string[] =>\n    (\n      JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(dir, \"manifest.json\"), \"utf8\")) as {\n        outputs: Array<{ path: string }>;\n      }\n    ).outputs.map((f) => f.path.split(\"/\").slice(1).join(\"/\"));\n  const lines = changedLines(before, after).filter((c) => c.file !== \"manifest.json\");\n  if (JSON.stringify(names(before)) !== JSON.stringify(names(after)))\n    lines.push({ file: \"manifest.json\", line: \"<file list differs>\" });\n  return lines;\n}\n\nconst changes = new WeakMap<ScenarioState, Array<{ file: string; line: string }>>();\n\nGiven(\"a scratch copy of {string}\", async ({ scenario }, path: string) => {\n  const scratch = scratchTempDir(\"vs4-tokens\");\n  scenario.cleanups.push(() => scratch.remove());\n  const tokens = join(scratch.dir, \"tokens.json\");\n  cpSync(repoPath(path), tokens);\n  scratches.set(scenario, {\n    root: scratch.dir,\n    tokens,\n    baselineOut: join(scratch.dir, \"out-before\"),\n    out: join(scratch.dir, \"out-after\"),\n  });\n});\n\nGiven(\n  \"the generator outputs for the unmodified scratch copy are recorded in a scratch directory\",\n  async ({ scenario, $testInfo }) => {\n    const s = scratchOf(scenario);\n    await runAndRecord(scenario, (n, o) => $testInfo.attach(n, o), generateInto(s, s.baselineOut));\n    expect(lastRun(scenario).exitCode, combinedOutput(lastRun(scenario))).toBe(0);\n    expect(listFiles(s.baselineOut).length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n  },\n);\n\nWhen(\n  \"the dark theme token {string} is changed to {string} in the scratch copy\",\n  async ({ scenario }, token: string, value: string) => {\n    const s = scratchOf(scenario);\n    const doc = JSON.parse(readFileSync(s.tokens, \"utf8\")) as {\n      themes: { dark: Record<string, string> };\n    };\n    expect(doc.themes.dark[token], `token ${token} exists`).toBeDefined();\n    doc.themes.dark[token] = value;\n    writeFileSync(s.tokens, `${JSON.stringify(doc, null, 2)}\\n`);\n  },\n);\n\nWhen(\n  \"the generator runs with {string} on the scratch copy\",\n  async ({ scenario, $testInfo }, command: string) => {\n    expect(command).toBe(\"pnpm --filter @know-meet/design-tokens generate\");\n    const s = scratchOf(scenario);\n    await runAndRecord(scenario, (n, o) => $testInfo.attach(n, o), generateInto(s, s.out));\n    changes.set(\n      scenario,\n      lastRun(scenario).exitCode === 0 ? tokenOutputChanges(s.baselineOut, s.out) : [],\n    );\n  },\n);\n\nWhen(\"the generator runs on the scratch copy\", async ({ scenario, $testInfo }) => {\n  const s = scratchOf(scenario);\n  await runAndRecord(scenario, (n, o) => $testInfo.attach(n, o), generateInto(s, s.out));\n});\n\nWhen(\n  \"the generator runs on the scratch copy with an output directory that does not exist\",\n  async ({ scenario, $testInfo }) => {\n    const s = scratchOf(scenario);\n    await runAndRecord(\n      scenario,\n      (n, o) => $testInfo.attach(n, o),\n      generateInto(s, join(s.root, \"missing\", \"out\"), false),\n    );\n  },\n);\n\nconst changedOf = (scenario: ScenarioState): Array<{ file: string; line: string }> =>\n  changes.get(scenario) ?? [];\n\nThen(\n  \"the web CSS variable {string} for the dark theme is {string}\",\n  async ({ scenario }, variable: string, value: string) => {\n    const hit = changedOf(scenario).find(\n      (c) =>\n        c.file.endsWith(\".css\") &&\n        c.line.includes(`${variable}:`) &&\n        c.line.toLowerCase().includes(value.toLowerCase()),\n    );\n    expect(hit, `a changed CSS line sets ${variable} to ${value}`).toBeDefined();\n  },\n);\n\nThen(\n  \"the Tailwind theme value for {string} in the dark theme is {string}\",\n  async ({ scenario }, token: string, value: string) => {\n    const s = scratchOf(scenario);\n    const themeFiles = listFiles(s.out).filter(\n      (f) => f.endsWith(\".css\") && readFileSync(join(s.out, f), \"utf8\").includes(\"@theme\"),\n    );\n    expect(themeFiles.length, \"a Tailwind @theme output exists\").toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    const text = themeFiles\n      .map((f) => readFileSync(join(s.out, f), \"utf8\"))\n      .join(\"\\n\")\n      .toLowerCase();\n    expect(text).toMatch(\n      new RegExp(`--color-${token}\\\\s*:\\\\s*(${value.toLowerCase()}|var\\\\(--${token}\\\\))`),\n    );\n  },\n);\n\nThen(\n  \"the Dart dark-theme constant for {string} is the colour {word}\",\n  async ({ scenario }, token: string, colour: string) => {\n    const hit = changedOf(scenario).find(\n      (c) => c.file.endsWith(\".dart\") && c.line.toUpperCase().includes(colour.toUpperCase()),\n    );\n    expect(hit, `a changed Dart line for ${token} holds ${colour}`).toBeDefined();\n  },\n);\n\nThen(\"no other output line differs from the recorded outputs\", async ({ scenario, $testInfo }) => {\n  const all = changedOf(scenario);\n  await $testInfo.attach(\"vs-4-output-diff.json\", {\n    body: JSON.stringify(all, null, 2),\n    contentType: \"application/json\",\n  });\n  const unrelated = all.filter((c) => !/123456/i.test(c.line));\n  expect(unrelated).toEqual([]);\n  expect(\n    new Set(all.map((c) => c.file.split(\".\").pop())).size,\n    \"CSS and Dart outputs changed\",\n  ).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(2);\n});\n\nThen(\"its error output names the token {string}\", async ({ scenario }, token: string) => {\n  expect(combinedOutput(lastRun(scenario))).toContain(token);\n});\n\nThen(\"no output file is written\", async ({ scenario }) => {\n  expect(existsSync(join(scratchOf(scenario).root, \"missing\"))).toBe(false);\n});\n",
    "tests/fidelity/steps/fidelity.steps.ts": "import { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { type Browser, expect, type Locator, type Page } from \"@playwright/test\";\nimport { CAPTURE_ENVIRONMENT } from \"../src/support/capture-environment.ts\";\nimport { sha256 } from \"../src/support/digests.ts\";\nimport {\n  baselineRelPath,\n  findEntry,\n  type Inventory,\n  type Theme,\n} from \"../src/support/inventory.ts\";\nimport { type FidelityOracle, loggedDefect, thresholdFor } from \"../src/support/oracle.ts\";\nimport { renderCell } from \"../src/support/render-cell.ts\";\nimport { BASELINES_DIR, FEATURES_DIR, repoPath } from \"../src/support/repo-paths.ts\";\nimport { runCommand, startServer } from \"../src/support/run-command.ts\";\nimport { createScratchWorktree, installScratch } from \"../src/support/scratch-worktree.ts\";\nimport { captureSubject, type RenderTarget } from \"../src/support/state-drivers.ts\";\nimport { Given, inScopeIdsOf, Then, When } from \"./fixtures.ts\";\n\nconst THEMES: readonly Theme[] = [\"dark\", \"light\"];\nconst VIEWPORTS: readonly number[] = [375, 768, 1024, 1440];\nconst SCRATCH_PREVIEW_PORT = 4174;\n\ntype ThemeValues = Record<string, Record<string, string>>;\n\nconst snapshotName = (rel: string): string[] => rel.split(\"/\");\n\n/** Compares one rendered cell with its baseline; throws (hard) or records (soft). */\nasync function compareCell(\n  subject: Page | Locator,\n  fullPage: boolean,\n  rel: string,\n  oracle: FidelityOracle,\n  stateId: string,\n  soft: boolean,\n): Promise<void> {\n  const limits = thresholdFor(oracle, stateId);\n  const options = {\n    ...CAPTURE_ENVIRONMENT.screenshot,\n    maxDiffPixelRatio: limits.maxDiffPixelRatio,\n    threshold: limits.threshold,\n    ...(fullPage ? { fullPage: true } : {}),\n  };\n  const assertion = soft ? expect.soft(subject) : expect(subject);\n  await assertion.toHaveScreenshot(snapshotName(rel), options);\n}\n\nasync function renderAndCompare(\n  browser: Browser,\n  target: RenderTarget,\n  inventory: Inventory,\n  oracle: FidelityOracle,\n  stateId: string,\n  soft: boolean,\n  exceeded: string[],\n): Promise<void> {\n  const entry = findEntry(inventory, stateId);\n  for (const theme of THEMES) {\n    for (const viewport of VIEWPORTS) {\n      const cell = await renderCell(browser, target, entry, theme, viewport);\n      if (cell === null) continue;\n      const rel = baselineRelPath(stateId, theme, viewport);\n      try {\n        expect.soft(cell.blocked, `external requests from ${rel}`).toEqual([]);\n        const { subject, fullPage } = captureSubject(cell.page, target, cell.plan);\n        const defect = loggedDefect(oracle, `${stateId}/${theme}/${viewport}`);\n        expect\n          .soft(defect, `design-lead logged a fidelity defect for ${rel} before the run`)\n          .toBeUndefined();\n        if (soft) await compareCell(subject, fullPage, rel, oracle, stateId, true);\n        else {\n          try {\n            await compareCell(subject, fullPage, rel, oracle, stateId, false);\n          } catch {\n            exceeded.push(rel);\n          }\n        }\n      } finally {\n        await cell.context.close();\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nGiven(\"the frozen fidelity oracle {string}\", async ({ oracle }, path: string) => {\n  expect(path).toBe(\"tests/fidelity/oracle/thresholds.json\");\n  expect(oracle.status).toBe(\"frozen\");\n});\n\nGiven(\"the prototype baselines recorded in {string}\", async ({ manifest }, path: string) => {\n  expect(path).toBe(\"tests/fidelity/baselines/manifest.json\");\n  expect(manifest.schema).toBe(\"know-meet-baselines/v1\");\n  expect(manifest.counts.failed, \"baseline capture failures\").toBe(0);\n});\n\nThen(\n  \"every in-scope inventory state has a baseline for each theme and viewport or a recorded not-applicable reason\",\n  async ({ inventory, manifest }) => {\n    const captured = new Set(\n      manifest.baselines.map((b) => `${b.stateId}/${b.theme}/${b.viewport}`),\n    );\n    const notApplicable = new Set(\n      manifest.skipped\n        .filter((s) => s.disposition === \"not-applicable\")\n        .map((s) => `${s.stateId}/${s.theme}/${s.viewport}`),\n    );\n    const missing = inScopeIdsOf(inventory)\n      .flatMap((entry) =>\n        THEMES.flatMap((theme) => VIEWPORTS.map((viewport) => `${entry.id}/${theme}/${viewport}`)),\n      )\n      .filter((cell) => !captured.has(cell) && !notApplicable.has(cell));\n    expect(missing).toEqual([]);\n  },\n);\n\nThen(\"every baseline image matches the sha256 recorded in the manifest\", async ({ manifest }) => {\n  const drifted = manifest.baselines\n    .filter((b) => sha256(readFileSync(join(BASELINES_DIR, b.path))) !== b.sha256)\n    .map((b) => b.path);\n  expect(drifted).toEqual([]);\n});\n\nThen(\n  \"the states listed in this feature are exactly the in-scope inventory states\",\n  async ({ inventory }) => {\n    const feature = readFileSync(join(FEATURES_DIR, \"vs-1-web-fidelity.feature\"), \"utf8\");\n    const examples = feature.slice(feature.indexOf(\"Examples:\"));\n    const listed = [...examples.matchAll(/^\\s*\\|\\s*([a-z0-9.-]+)\\s*\\|\\s*$/gm)]\n      .map((m) => m[1])\n      .filter((id) => id !== \"state\");\n    expect([...listed].sort()).toEqual(\n      inScopeIdsOf(inventory)\n        .map((e) => e.id)\n        .sort(),\n    );\n  },\n);\n\nWhen(\n  \"the web app renders state {string} in each theme at each viewport\",\n  async ({ browser, appTarget, inventory, oracle, scenario }, stateId: string) => {\n    scenario.exceededCells = [];\n    await renderAndCompare(\n      browser,\n      appTarget,\n      inventory,\n      oracle,\n      stateId,\n      true,\n      scenario.exceededCells,\n    );\n  },\n);\n\nThen(\n  \"every capture of {string} is within its frozen threshold of the prototype baseline\",\n  async ({ $testInfo }, stateId: string) => {\n    const failures = $testInfo.errors.map((e) => e.message ?? \"\").filter((m) => m.length > 0);\n    expect(failures, `soft comparison failures for ${stateId}`).toEqual([]);\n  },\n);\n\nGiven(\n  \"a scratch web build whose tokens.json is the pre-reconciliation version from commit {string}\",\n  async ({ scenario, $testInfo }, commit: string) => {\n    const tree = createScratchWorktree(\"vs1-old-tokens\");\n    scenario.cleanups.push(() => tree.remove());\n    await $testInfo.attach(\"negative-control-candidate.json\", {\n      body: tree.candidateReceipt,\n      contentType: \"application/json\",\n    });\n    const old = runCommand(`git show ${commit}:docs/design/tokens.json`);\n    expect(old.exitCode, old.stderr).toBe(0);\n    expect(sha256(old.stdout), \"the control must use different tokens\").not.toBe(\n      sha256(readFileSync(repoPath(\"docs/design/tokens.json\"))),\n    );\n    // The generator now requires the current document shape (fonts, 220+ keys), which the\n    // pre-reconciliation file predates. The control keeps the current structure and puts the\n    // pre-reconciliation value back on every key both documents define.\n    const oldThemes = (JSON.parse(old.stdout) as { themes: ThemeValues }).themes;\n    const current = JSON.parse(\n      readFileSync(join(tree.dir, \"docs\", \"design\", \"tokens.json\"), \"utf8\"),\n    ) as { themes: ThemeValues };\n    let reverted = 0;\n    for (const [theme, values] of Object.entries(oldThemes)) {\n      for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(values)) {\n        const target = current.themes[theme];\n        if (target !== undefined && key in target && target[key] !== value) {\n          target[key] = value;\n          reverted += 1;\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    expect(\n      reverted,\n      \"pre-reconciliation values that differ from the current tokens\",\n    ).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    writeFileSync(\n      join(tree.dir, \"docs\", \"design\", \"tokens.json\"),\n      `${JSON.stringify(current, null, 2)}\\n`,\n    );\n    installScratch(tree.dir);\n    for (const command of [\n      \"pnpm --filter @know-meet/design-tokens generate\",\n      \"pnpm --filter @know-meet/web build\",\n    ]) {\n      const run = runCommand(command, tree.dir);\n      expect(run.exitCode, `${command}\\n${run.stderr.slice(-3000)}`).toBe(0);\n    }\n    const url = `http://127.0.0.1:${SCRATCH_PREVIEW_PORT}`;\n    const server = await startServer(\n      `pnpm --filter @know-meet/web preview --host 127.0.0.1 --port ${SCRATCH_PREVIEW_PORT} --strictPort`,\n      tree.dir,\n      url,\n    );\n    scenario.cleanups.push(() => server.stop());\n    scenario.scratchDir = tree.dir;\n    scenario.scratchBaseUrl = url;\n  },\n);\n\nWhen(\n  \"that build renders states {string}, {string} and {string} in each theme at each viewport\",\n  async ({ browser, appTarget, inventory, oracle, scenario }, a: string, b: string, c: string) => {\n    const base = scenario.scratchBaseUrl ?? \"\";\n    const scratchTarget: RenderTarget = {\n      ...appTarget,\n      urlFor: (entry) => {\n        const url = new URL(appTarget.urlFor(entry));\n        return `${base}${url.pathname}${url.search}${url.hash}`;\n      },\n    };\n    scenario.exceededCells = [];\n    for (const stateId of [a, b, c])\n      await renderAndCompare(\n        browser,\n        scratchTarget,\n        inventory,\n        oracle,\n        stateId,\n        false,\n        scenario.exceededCells,\n      );\n  },\n);\n\nThen(\"at least one capture exceeds its frozen threshold\", async ({ scenario, $testInfo }) => {\n  await $testInfo.attach(\"negative-control cells over threshold\", {\n    body: JSON.stringify(scenario.exceededCells ?? []),\n    contentType: \"application/json\",\n  });\n  expect((scenario.exceededCells ?? []).length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n});\n\nWhen(\n  \"the dark baseline of {string} at {int} is compared with its light baseline under the frozen threshold\",\n  async ({ oracle, scenario }, stateId: string, viewport: number) => {\n    const dark = readFileSync(join(BASELINES_DIR, baselineRelPath(stateId, \"dark\", viewport)));\n    const limits = thresholdFor(oracle, stateId);\n    try {\n      expect(dark).toMatchSnapshot(snapshotName(baselineRelPath(stateId, \"light\", viewport)), {\n        maxDiffPixelRatio: limits.maxDiffPixelRatio,\n        threshold: limits.threshold,\n      });\n      scenario.comparisonFailed = false;\n    } catch {\n      scenario.comparisonFailed = true;\n    }\n  },\n);\n\nThen(\"the comparison fails\", async ({ scenario }) => {\n  expect(scenario.comparisonFailed).toBe(true);\n});\n",
    "packages/ui/src/components/tabs.tsx": "// TJ-ARCH-MOB-001 compliant\n// Two prototype controls on one primitive, migrated to tokens v1.3.0 (D-6):\n//   TabsList variant default   \u2192 km.css `.tabs`: no list rule, no underline. Tabs\n//                                are transparent `fg-sub` text (the text identifies\n//                                them), hover `card-hov`, the active tab is a\n//                                `selected` pill with `on-selected` text.\n//   TabsList variant segmented \u2192 DESIGN.md segmented control: `control` track,\n//                                `on-control` segments, active `selected` with a\n//                                leading check icon.\n// Focus is the `focus` fill on every tab and on a focused panel (lib/focus.ts).\nimport { Tabs as TabsPrimitive } from \"@base-ui/react/tabs\";\nimport { cva, type VariantProps } from \"class-variance-authority\";\nimport { CheckIcon } from \"lucide-react\";\nimport type * as React from \"react\";\nimport { focusFillClass } from \"#lib/focus\";\nimport { cn } from \"#lib/utils\";\n\nfunction Tabs({ className, orientation = \"horizontal\", ...props }: TabsPrimitive.Root.Props) {\n  return (\n    <TabsPrimitive.Root\n      data-slot=\"tabs\"\n      data-orientation={orientation}\n      className={cn(\"group/tabs flex gap-s4 data-[orientation=horizontal]:flex-col\", className)}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\nconst tabsListVariants = cva(\n  \"group/tabs-list flex group-data-[orientation=vertical]/tabs:flex-col\",\n  {\n    variants: {\n      variant: {\n        default:\n          \"w-full gap-s1 overflow-x-auto [scrollbar-width:none] group-data-[orientation=vertical]/tabs:w-fit [&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden\",\n        segmented: \"inline-flex w-fit flex-wrap gap-1 rounded-base bg-control p-1\",\n      },\n    },\n    defaultVariants: {\n      variant: \"default\",\n    },\n  },\n);\n\nfunction TabsList({\n  className,\n  variant = \"default\",\n  ...props\n}: TabsPrimitive.List.Props & VariantProps<typeof tabsListVariants>) {\n  return (\n    <TabsPrimitive.List\n      data-slot=\"tabs-list\"\n      data-variant={variant}\n      className={cn(tabsListVariants({ variant }), className)}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\nfunction TabsTrigger({ className, children, ...props }: TabsPrimitive.Tab.Props) {\n  return (\n    <TabsPrimitive.Tab\n      data-slot=\"tabs-trigger\"\n      className={cn(\n        \"group/tabs-trigger inline-flex flex-none items-center gap-1.5 bg-transparent text-sm font-semibold whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[color,background-color] duration-(--dur-fast) ease-standard disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50 aria-disabled:cursor-not-allowed aria-disabled:opacity-50 data-active:bg-selected data-active:text-on-selected [&_svg]:pointer-events-none [&_svg]:shrink-0 [&_svg:not([class*='size-'])]:size-4\",\n        \"group-data-[variant=default]/tabs-list:min-h-size-target group-data-[variant=default]/tabs-list:rounded-pill group-data-[variant=default]/tabs-list:px-s4 group-data-[variant=default]/tabs-list:text-muted-foreground group-data-[variant=default]/tabs-list:hover:not-data-active:bg-accent group-data-[variant=default]/tabs-list:hover:not-data-active:text-foreground\",\n        \"group-data-[variant=segmented]/tabs-list:min-h-size-control-h-sm group-data-[variant=segmented]/tabs-list:rounded-9 group-data-[variant=segmented]/tabs-list:px-s3 group-data-[variant=segmented]/tabs-list:text-on-control group-data-[variant=segmented]/tabs-list:hover:not-data-active:bg-control-hov\",\n        focusFillClass,\n        className,\n      )}\n      {...props}\n    >\n      <CheckIcon\n        aria-hidden=\"true\"\n        data-slot=\"tabs-trigger-check\"\n        className=\"hidden group-data-[variant=segmented]/tabs-list:group-data-active/tabs-trigger:inline-block\"\n      />\n      {children}\n    </TabsPrimitive.Tab>\n  );\n}\n\n/** km.css `.tabs .count`: a mono count pill inside a tab label (inherits the tab text colour). */\nfunction TabsCount({ className, ...props }: React.ComponentProps<\"span\">) {\n  return (\n    <span\n      data-slot=\"tabs-count\"\n      className={cn(\n        \"rounded-pill bg-muted px-1.5 py-px font-mono text-11 text-muted-foreground group-data-active/tabs-trigger:bg-transparent group-data-active/tabs-trigger:text-current group-focus-visible/tabs-trigger:bg-transparent group-focus-visible/tabs-trigger:text-current\",\n        className,\n      )}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\n/** A focused panel takes the focus fill like a focused card (DESIGN.md \"Interactive card\"). */\nfunction TabsContent({ className, ...props }: TabsPrimitive.Panel.Props) {\n  return (\n    <TabsPrimitive.Panel\n      data-slot=\"tabs-content\"\n      className={cn(\"flex-1 rounded-base\", focusFillClass, className)}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\nexport { Tabs, TabsContent, TabsCount, TabsList, TabsTrigger, tabsListVariants };\n",
    "packages/ui/src/components/toast.tsx": "// TJ-ARCH-MOB-001 compliant\n// km.css `.toasts` / `.toast`: a centred stack 32px above the bottom (16px under\n// 768px, plus the bottom bar `--km-bottom-bar-h` when the frame shows one), max\n// `size-toast-w`; actions focus to the page ground (inverted surface); each toast is inverted (fg fill, bg text), radius, float\n// shadow. Base UI stacking and swipe mechanics are kept; timings use the motion\n// tokens (--dur in with --ease-out).\nimport { Toast as ToastPrimitive } from \"@base-ui/react/toast\";\nimport {\n  CheckIcon,\n  InfoIcon,\n  Loader2Icon,\n  OctagonXIcon,\n  TriangleAlertIcon,\n  XIcon,\n} from \"lucide-react\";\nimport type * as React from \"react\";\nimport { Button } from \"#components/button\";\nimport { invertedFocusFillClass } from \"#lib/focus\";\nimport { cn } from \"#lib/utils\";\n\nconst toast = ToastPrimitive.createToastManager();\n\nfunction ToastProvider({ ...props }: ToastPrimitive.Provider.Props) {\n  return <ToastPrimitive.Provider {...props} />;\n}\n\nfunction ToastPortal({ ...props }: ToastPrimitive.Portal.Props) {\n  return <ToastPrimitive.Portal data-slot=\"toast-portal\" {...props} />;\n}\n\nfunction ToastViewport({ className, ...props }: ToastPrimitive.Viewport.Props) {\n  return (\n    <ToastPrimitive.Viewport\n      data-slot=\"toast-viewport\"\n      className={cn(\n        \"pointer-events-none fixed inset-x-0 bottom-s6 z-(--z-toast) mx-auto w-[min(var(--spacing-size-toast-w),calc(100vw-32px))] outline-none max-bp768:bottom-[calc(var(--km-bottom-bar-h,0px)+var(--spacing-s4))]\",\n        className,\n      )}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\nfunction Toast({ className, ...props }: ToastPrimitive.Root.Props) {\n  return (\n    <ToastPrimitive.Root\n      data-slot=\"toast\"\n      className={cn(\n        \"group/toast pointer-events-auto absolute right-0 bottom-0 z-[calc(1000-var(--toast-index))] w-full origin-bottom rounded-base bg-foreground text-background shadow-(--shadow-float) will-change-transform select-none\",\n        \"[--gap:var(--s2)] [--height:var(--toast-frontmost-height,var(--toast-height))] [--offset-y:calc(var(--toast-offset-y)*-1+calc(var(--toast-index)*var(--gap)*-1)+var(--toast-swipe-movement-y))] [--peek:var(--s3)] [--scale:calc(max(0,1-(var(--toast-index)*0.1)))] [--shrink:calc(1-var(--scale))]\",\n        \"h-(--height) [transform:translateX(var(--toast-swipe-movement-x))_translateY(calc(var(--toast-swipe-movement-y)-(var(--toast-index)*var(--peek))-(var(--shrink)*var(--height))))_scale(var(--scale))] [transition:transform_var(--dur)_var(--ease-out),opacity_var(--dur)_var(--ease-out),height_var(--dur-fast)_var(--ease-standard)]\",\n        \"after:absolute after:top-full after:left-0 after:h-[calc(var(--gap)+1px)] after:w-full after:content-['']\",\n        \"data-expanded:h-(--toast-height) data-expanded:[transform:translateX(var(--toast-swipe-movement-x))_translateY(var(--offset-y))]\",\n        \"data-limited:opacity-0 data-starting-style:[transform:translateY(150%)]\",\n        \"[&[data-ending-style]:not([data-limited]):not([data-swipe-direction])]:[transform:translateY(150%)]\",\n        \"data-ending-style:data-[swipe-direction=down]:[transform:translateY(calc(var(--toast-swipe-movement-y)+150%))]\",\n        \"data-ending-style:data-[swipe-direction=left]:[transform:translateX(calc(var(--toast-swipe-movement-x)-150%))_translateY(var(--offset-y))]\",\n        \"data-ending-style:data-[swipe-direction=right]:[transform:translateX(calc(var(--toast-swipe-movement-x)+150%))_translateY(var(--offset-y))]\",\n        \"data-ending-style:data-[swipe-direction=up]:[transform:translateY(calc(var(--toast-swipe-movement-y)-150%))]\",\n        \"data-expanded:data-ending-style:data-[swipe-direction=down]:[transform:translateY(calc(var(--toast-swipe-movement-y)+150%))]\",\n        \"data-expanded:data-ending-style:data-[swipe-direction=left]:[transform:translateX(calc(var(--toast-swipe-movement-x)-150%))_translateY(var(--offset-y))]\",\n        \"data-expanded:data-ending-style:data-[swipe-direction=right]:[transform:translateX(calc(var(--toast-swipe-movement-x)+150%))_translateY(var(--offset-y))]\",\n        \"data-expanded:data-ending-style:data-[swipe-direction=up]:[transform:translateY(calc(var(--toast-swipe-movement-y)-150%))]\",\n        className,\n      )}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\nfunction ToastContent({ className, ...props }: ToastPrimitive.Content.Props) {\n  return (\n    <ToastPrimitive.Content\n      data-slot=\"toast-content\"\n      className={cn(\n        \"flex h-full items-center gap-s2 overflow-hidden px-s4 py-s3 transition-opacity duration-(--dur) ease-out data-behind:opacity-0 data-expanded:opacity-100\",\n        className,\n      )}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\nfunction ToastTitle({ className, ...props }: ToastPrimitive.Title.Props) {\n  return (\n    <ToastPrimitive.Title\n      data-slot=\"toast-title\"\n      className={cn(\"text-sm font-medium text-background\", className)}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\nfunction ToastDescription({ className, ...props }: ToastPrimitive.Description.Props) {\n  return (\n    <ToastPrimitive.Description\n      data-slot=\"toast-description\"\n      className={cn(\"text-sm font-regular text-background\", className)}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\nfunction ToastAction({\n  className,\n  render = <Button variant=\"ghost\" size=\"sm\" />,\n  ...props\n}: ToastPrimitive.Action.Props) {\n  return (\n    <ToastPrimitive.Action\n      data-slot=\"toast-action\"\n      render={render}\n      className={cn(\n        \"shrink-0 text-background underline underline-offset-[3px] hover:not-disabled:bg-[color-mix(in_srgb,var(--background)_14%,transparent)]\",\n        invertedFocusFillClass,\n        className,\n      )}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\nfunction ToastClose({\n  className,\n  children,\n  render = <Button variant=\"ghost\" size=\"icon-sm\" />,\n  ...props\n}: ToastPrimitive.Close.Props) {\n  return (\n    <ToastPrimitive.Close\n      data-slot=\"toast-close\"\n      aria-label=\"Close toast\"\n      render={render}\n      className={cn(\n        \"relative shrink-0 text-background after:absolute after:-inset-2 after:content-[''] hover:not-disabled:bg-[color-mix(in_srgb,var(--background)_14%,transparent)]\",\n        invertedFocusFillClass,\n        className,\n      )}\n      {...props}\n    >\n      {children ?? <XIcon aria-hidden=\"true\" />}\n    </ToastPrimitive.Close>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction ToastIcon({ type }: { type: string | undefined }) {\n  let icon: React.ReactNode = null;\n\n  if (type === \"success\") {\n    icon = <CheckIcon aria-hidden=\"true\" />;\n  }\n\n  if (type === \"info\") {\n    icon = <InfoIcon aria-hidden=\"true\" />;\n  }\n\n  if (type === \"warning\") {\n    icon = <TriangleAlertIcon aria-hidden=\"true\" />;\n  }\n\n  if (type === \"error\") {\n    icon = <OctagonXIcon className=\"text-red\" aria-hidden=\"true\" />;\n  }\n\n  if (type === \"loading\") {\n    icon = (\n      <Loader2Icon\n        className=\"animate-spin [animation-duration:var(--anim-spin)]\"\n        aria-hidden=\"true\"\n      />\n    );\n  }\n\n  if (!icon) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <span\n      data-slot=\"toast-icon\"\n      className=\"shrink-0 [&_svg]:pointer-events-none [&_svg:not([class*='size-'])]:size-5\"\n    >\n      {icon}\n    </span>\n  );\n}\n\nfunction ToastList({ dismissible }: { readonly dismissible: boolean }) {\n  const { toasts } = ToastPrimitive.useToastManager();\n\n  return toasts.map((toastItem) => (\n    <Toast key={toastItem.id} toast={toastItem}>\n      <ToastContent>\n        <ToastIcon type={toastItem.type} />\n        <div className=\"flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-1\">\n          <ToastTitle />\n          <ToastDescription />\n        </div>\n        <ToastAction />\n        {dismissible ? <ToastClose /> : null}\n      </ToastContent>\n    </Toast>\n  ));\n}\n\nfunction Toaster({\n  children,\n  toastManager = toast,\n  viewportClassName,\n  dismissible = true,\n  ...props\n}: ToastPrimitive.Provider.Props & {\n  readonly viewportClassName?: string;\n  readonly dismissible?: boolean;\n}) {\n  return (\n    <ToastProvider toastManager={toastManager} {...props}>\n      {children}\n      <ToastPortal>\n        <ToastViewport className={viewportClassName}>\n          <ToastList dismissible={dismissible} />\n        </ToastViewport>\n      </ToastPortal>\n    </ToastProvider>\n  );\n}\n\nconst createToastManager = ToastPrimitive.createToastManager;\nconst useToastManager = ToastPrimitive.useToastManager;\n\nexport {\n  createToastManager,\n  Toast,\n  ToastAction,\n  ToastClose,\n  ToastContent,\n  ToastDescription,\n  Toaster,\n  ToastPortal,\n  ToastProvider,\n  ToastTitle,\n  ToastViewport,\n  toast,\n  useToastManager,\n};\n",
    "apps/web/src/presentation/meeting-room/presentation/meeting-room-screen.tsx": "// TJ-ARCH-MOB-001 compliant\n// c11 task 11.5: the meeting-room layout (meet.html #room and #room-guest) with\n// media stubbed. RoomLayout gives this screen <main id=\"main\"> and no app bar; the\n// room owns its chrome: head, participant stage with captions, control bar.\n// Out of scope this phase (D-2): side panels, #start, #lobby, #ended and\n// #processing. Any other hash renders the room for the current session (signed\n// in: full room; signed out: guest room), as meet.html `routeRoom` does for #room.\nimport { Toaster, toast } from \"@know-meet/ui/components/toast\";\nimport { focusFillClass } from \"@know-meet/ui/lib/focus\";\nimport { cn } from \"@know-meet/ui/lib/utils\";\nimport type * as React from \"react\";\nimport { useCallback, useEffect, useMemo, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useSessionUser } from \"../../shared/session\";\nimport { useDocumentTitle } from \"../../shared/use-document-title\";\nimport { useHashRoute } from \"../../shared/use-hash-route\";\nimport { useSampleWorkspace } from \"../../workspace/use-workspace\";\nimport { buildRoomModel, roomModeFor } from \"../application/room-fixture\";\nimport type { RoomTile } from \"../domain/room\";\nimport { RoomControls } from \"./room-controls\";\nimport { RoomHead } from \"./room-head\";\nimport { RoomTileView, type TileActions } from \"./room-tiles\";\nimport { useStageLayout } from \"./use-stage-layout\";\n\n/** Applies the local control state (mic, camera, paused dot) to the fixture tiles. */\nfunction withLocalState(\n  tiles: readonly RoomTile[],\n  micOn: boolean,\n  cameraOn: boolean,\n  pausedDots: ReadonlySet<string>,\n): RoomTile[] {\n  return tiles.map((tile) => {\n    if (tile.kind === \"person\" && tile.isSelf) return { ...tile, muted: !micOn, cameraOn };\n    if (tile.kind === \"dot\" && pausedDots.has(tile.id)) return { ...tile, state: \"paused\" };\n    return tile;\n  });\n}\n\nfunction Captions() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex justify-center px-s5 pb-s3 max-bp768:px-s3 max-bp768:pb-s2\">\n      <div\n        aria-live=\"polite\"\n        className=\"grid min-h-[72px] w-[min(100%,760px)] gap-0.5 rounded-base bg-surface px-s4 py-s3 shadow-(--shadow-card)\"\n      >\n        <span className=\"block font-mono text-11 font-semibold tracking-[0.08em] text-muted-foreground uppercase\">\n          Captions\n        </span>\n        <span className=\"block leading-[1.5]\">Waiting for someone to speak\u2026</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nexport function MeetingRoomScreen({ themeControl }: { readonly themeControl: React.ReactNode }) {\n  const { view } = useHashRoute();\n  const user = useSessionUser();\n  const { workspace } = useSampleWorkspace();\n  const mode = roomModeFor(view, user !== null);\n  const room = useMemo(\n    () => buildRoomModel(workspace, mode, user?.name ?? null),\n    [workspace, mode, user],\n  );\n  useDocumentTitle(`Know Meet \u2014 ${room.title}`);\n\n  const [startedAt] = useState(() => Date.now());\n  const [micOn, setMicOn] = useState(true);\n  const [cameraOn, setCameraOn] = useState(false);\n  const [captionsOn, setCaptionsOn] = useState(true);\n  const [pausedDots, setPausedDots] = useState<ReadonlySet<string>>(() => new Set());\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const id = toast.add({\n      title: room.transcribing\n        ? \"You joined. Captions and transcription are on.\"\n        : \"You joined. Transcription is off.\",\n      type: \"success\",\n      timeout: 3400,\n    });\n    return () => toast.close(id);\n  }, [room.transcribing]);\n\n  const tiles = withLocalState(room.tiles, micOn, cameraOn, pausedDots);\n  const stageRef = useRef<HTMLElement>(null);\n  const stage = useStageLayout(stageRef, tiles.length);\n\n  const onUnavailable = useCallback((what: string) => {\n    toast.add({ title: `${what} opens in a later release.`, type: \"info\" });\n  }, []);\n  const actions = useMemo<TileActions>(\n    () => ({\n      onUnavailable,\n      onToggleDotPause: (id) =>\n        setPausedDots((prev) => {\n          const next = new Set(prev);\n          if (next.has(id)) next.delete(id);\n          else next.add(id);\n          return next;\n        }),\n    }),\n    [onUnavailable],\n  );\n\n  return (\n    <Toaster\n      dismissible={false}\n      viewportClassName=\"bottom-28 max-bp768:bottom-24 [&_[data-slot=toast-icon]_svg]:size-4\"\n    >\n      <div className=\"grid h-[calc(100dvh-var(--km-titlebar-h,0px))] grid-rows-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)_auto] overflow-hidden\">\n        <RoomHead\n          room={room}\n          participantCount={tiles.length}\n          onUnavailable={onUnavailable}\n          themeControl={themeControl}\n        />\n        <div className=\"relative grid min-h-0 grid-rows-[minmax(0,1fr)_auto]\">\n          <section\n            ref={stageRef}\n            aria-label=\"Participants\"\n            tabIndex={stage.scrollable ? 0 : undefined}\n            className={cn(\n              \"min-h-0 overflow-y-auto px-s5 pt-s2 pb-s4 max-bp768:px-s3 max-bp768:pb-s3\",\n              stage.scrollable &&\n                cn(\n                  focusFillClass,\n                  \"focus-visible:**:bg-transparent! focus-visible:**:text-inherit!\",\n                ),\n            )}\n          >\n            <ul\n              className=\"grid content-start gap-s3\"\n              style={{ gridTemplateColumns: `repeat(${stage.columns}, minmax(0, 1fr))` }}\n            >\n              {tiles.map((tile) => (\n                <RoomTileView key={tile.id} tile={tile} actions={actions} />\n              ))}\n            </ul>\n          </section>\n          {captionsOn ? <Captions /> : <div aria-hidden=\"true\" />}\n        </div>\n        <RoomControls\n          mode={room.mode}\n          startedAt={startedAt}\n          micOn={micOn}\n          cameraOn={cameraOn}\n          captionsOn={captionsOn}\n          onToggleMic={() => setMicOn((on) => !on)}\n          onToggleCamera={() => setCameraOn((on) => !on)}\n          onToggleCaptions={() => setCaptionsOn((on) => !on)}\n          onUnavailable={onUnavailable}\n        />\n      </div>\n    </Toaster>\n  );\n}\n"
  },
